+# ECLIPSE R7 FAIR-PLAY INTEGRATION GATE
+
+1. During an unfinished Gomoku game, ECLIPSE must NEVER suggest or highlight any next move.
+2. No live-board heat maps, danger points, candidate rings, arrows or PV lines.
+3. The thought graph is decorative and independent of real chess coordinates.
+4. Searcher raw PV/candidates stay private; UI receives only sanitized depth/node metrics.
+5. Actual replay unlocks only after the match has finished, in a separate read-only board.
+6. Replay must use validated saved moves, black/white alternation and matching final board.
+7. Do not rename or affect Grok avatars outside Gomoku.
+8. Hide unknown search metrics instead of manufacturing progress.
+9. Verify no stale trace survives match restart or seat changes.
+10. Resolve R5 search (#193/#196) and R6 UI (#197) overlaps before applying.
+11. Test full main patch/Xcode/XCTest/VoiceOver/mobile viewports and device touch handling.
+12. Do not delete old engines, alter release/version or merge without Governor permission.
